<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-3405] IGFS: Do not allow DUAL -&gt; PRIMARY -&gt; DUAL modes interleaving.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-3405</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Currently we allow almost any combinations of path modes. This appears to be wrong. Consider the following scenario:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1) /dir1 -&amp;gt; PRIMARY&lt;br/&gt;
2) /dir1/dir2 -&amp;gt; DUAL&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is impossible to support this scenario properly because &lt;tt&gt;dir1&lt;/tt&gt; will be created in both file systems anyway, but primary and secondary representation will be &quot;detached&quot; from each other.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead, we should allow only DUAL -&amp;gt; PRIMARY and DUAL -&amp;gt; PROXY transitions. Any other combinations doesn&apos;t make sense.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12985723">IGNITE-3405</key>
            <summary>IGFS: Do not allow DUAL -&gt; PRIMARY -&gt; DUAL modes interleaving.</summary>
